<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13282"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 5:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here are some very interesting blurbs I found in the police/fire sections of arkvalleynews.com <BR>---------------------------------------- <BR> <BR>2003-Sept. 28--Vickie Gansen reported the burglary of a residence at #245 Pueblo. Nothing was reported missing, but there was minor damage to a door, Officer Terry Love reported. <BR>------------------------------------------- <BR> <BR>---------------------------------------- <BR>&#40;this is Marines old house&#41; : <BR>Sept 2003-Heard Connie Pouyamehr, 6254 Independence, inquire about a $656.38 bill she received from the city for a meter stop replacement.  <BR> <BR>Pouyamehr said she called the city to have her water turned off when she discovered a leak Aug. 2. She said a city employee came and turned the meter and in doing so, the meter broke.  <BR> <BR>Whitson said the report he had heard was that the meter was broken when the employee arrived. If the employee was the one turning the meter when it broke, she should not have been charged, he said.  <BR> <BR>Pouyamehr said she was told never to touch the meter when she moved into her house in 1991, so she called the city and did not touch it.  <BR> <BR>The council told Whitson to talk to the employee about the incident.  <BR>&#40;I wonder which city employee this is?&#41; <BR>-------------------------------- <BR>2005-March 6--Officers Terrell Brown and Hobert Capps responded to the report of news media allegedly harassing an identified woman at 6314 N. Jacksonville. The media was across the street, taking photos of a residence, the officers reported. She was advised that as long as they were not on her property, they could take photos. No criminal activity was discovered. <BR>--------------------------------------- <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>&#40;NOTICE THE DATE!!&#41; <BR>2004-Jan. 14--An identified woman reported coming out of the bathroom and finding a man standing in her living room. She chased him from the house and noticed that her wallet was missing from her purse on the dining room table. Loss was estimated at $15 <BR>--------------------------------- <BR>2003-Aug. 8--8:35 p.m. Deputy Dana Hoffman responded to the report of a threatening letter <BR>-------------------------------------- <BR> <BR>&#40;WHAT IS THIS ABOUT????&#41; <BR>2003-Oct. 30--Capt. Dale Coffman notified the FBI of a letter received from a possibly identified person, and reported that the FBI would do the follow-up investigation. <BR>------------------------------------------ <BR>2003June 1--9:14 a.m. Christ Lutheran Church reported an identified man coming to the church and making disturbing statements to the congregation during the service at 5356 N. Hillside. Deputy Edward Clark was unable to locate the suspect <BR>------------------------------------------- <BR> <BR>Just some tidbits for y&#39;all. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13282-->
<!--Post: 13315--><!--Time: 1114908782-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13315"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 30, 2005 - 5:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty: I was really hoping that nobody would discover who lived in Marine&#39;s house. But, since you put it out there, Connie is a great lady. She is a hard working soul that is very frustrated with the lookyloos. Her and my Mom used to play bingo together and after one bingo session I was the person to inform her of the goings on at her house before she lived there. She was really taken back by it, and asked a lot of questions about Marine. It&#39;s funny because Connie and Marine had many things in common. I guess that&#39;s why Mom got along with her so well after she moved into Marine&#39;s house.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
